## psc/parse/diagnostics.pengu — diagnósticos sintácticos de F2.
##
## Todos los errores de sintaxis comparten el código `E0000`, igual que
## stage0. Lo que cambia es el mensaje, el `help` y el `note`, que aquí son
## específicos para que un humano sepa qué corregir.
##
## ## Memoria
## `parse_issue_message` devuelve un `string` owned. Los `help`/`note` son
## literales estáticos. `emit_parse_issue` copia lo que necesita el
## `DiagnosticBag` y libera el mensaje.

import std.diagnostic as diag

import psc.span as pspan
import psc.source as psource
import psc.diagnostics as psdiag

insignia psc_parse_diag_

## Código público de todos los errores sintácticos.
const PSC_E_SYNTAX as string is "E0000"

## Cada problema que puede detectar el parser.
omen ParseIssue:
    ## Falta un token concreto; `detail` dice cuál.
    ParseExpectedToken
    ## El token actual no puede empezar la construcción.
    ParseUnexpectedToken
    ## Se esperaba una expresión.
    ParseExpectedExpression
    ## Se esperaba un tipo.
    ParseExpectedType
    ## Se esperaba un nombre.
    ParseExpectedName
    ## Falta el `NEWLINE` de fin de statement.
    ParseExpectedNewline
    ## Falta el `INDENT` de un bloque.
    ParseExpectedIndent
    ## Falta el `DEDENT` de un bloque.
    ParseExpectedDedent
    ## Un bloque `:` no tiene ningún statement.
    ParseEmptyBlock
    ## Varios statements en una línea sin separador.
    ParseMultipleStatements
    ## `and` usado como separador donde ya no lo es.
    ParseLegacyAndSeparator
    ## `set xs at n - 1 is v`: el índice necesita paréntesis.
    ParseAtIndexPrecedence
    ## Demasiados delimitadores/expresiones anidadas.
    ParseMaxDepth
    ## Demasiados bloques anidados.
    ParseMaxBlockDepth
    ## El target de un `set` no es asignable.
    ParseInvalidSetTarget
    ## El target de un `calling` no es válido.
    ParseInvalidCallTarget
    ## Atributo mal formado.
    ParseInvalidAttribute
    ## Lista de `declare` mal formada.
    ParseInvalidDeclareParams
    ## Cláusula `when` mal formada.
    ParseInvalidWhenClause
    ## Tipo mal formado.
    ParseInvalidType
    ## Fin de archivo inesperado.
    ParseUnexpectedEof

## Mensaje principal de un issue.
##
## `detail` se interpola solo en los issues que lo necesitan. El resultado es
## owned; el llamador lo libera.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un `string` owned; liberar con `banish`.
weave parse_issue_message with issue as ParseIssue, detail as string into string:
    var msg as string is judge issue:
        when ParseExpectedToken -> "expected {detail}"
        when ParseUnexpectedToken -> "unexpected {detail}"
        when ParseExpectedExpression -> "expected an expression"
        when ParseExpectedType -> "expected a type"
        when ParseExpectedName -> "expected a name"
        when ParseExpectedNewline -> "expected a newline after the statement"
        when ParseExpectedIndent -> "expected an indented block"
        when ParseExpectedDedent -> "expected the end of the block"
        when ParseEmptyBlock -> "a block must contain at least one statement"
        when ParseMultipleStatements -> "Syntax error: multiple statements on a single line require a newline delimiter"
        when ParseLegacyAndSeparator -> "'and' is no longer a separator: use ',' (offending 'and' at {detail})"
        when ParseAtIndexPrecedence -> "The index after 'at' binds tighter than '{detail}': parenthesise the index expression"
        when ParseMaxDepth -> "Source nesting exceeds the maximum supported depth ({detail})"
        when ParseMaxBlockDepth -> "Block nesting exceeds the maximum supported depth ({detail})"
        when ParseInvalidSetTarget -> "invalid assignment target"
        when ParseInvalidCallTarget -> "invalid call target"
        when ParseInvalidAttribute -> "invalid attribute"
        when ParseInvalidDeclareParams -> "invalid declare parameter list"
        when ParseInvalidWhenClause -> "invalid 'when' clause"
        when ParseInvalidType -> "invalid type"
        when ParseUnexpectedEof -> "unexpected end of file"
    return msg

## Texto de ayuda del issue ("" si no tiene).
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un literal estático; no liberar.
weave parse_issue_help with issue as ParseIssue into string:
    return judge issue:
        when ParseExpectedToken -> "Check the syntax around this position (see LANGUAGE.md / CHEATSHEET.md)."
        when ParseUnexpectedToken -> "Check the syntax around this position (see LANGUAGE.md / CHEATSHEET.md)."
        when ParseExpectedExpression -> "Write an expression after the operator or keyword."
        when ParseExpectedType -> "Write a type such as 'int', 'list of T' or 'ref to T'."
        when ParseExpectedName -> "Write an identifier."
        when ParseExpectedNewline -> "Put one statement per line, or use ':' for a single-line block."
        when ParseExpectedIndent -> "Indent the block one level (four spaces) after the ':'."
        when ParseExpectedDedent -> "Check the indentation; the block never returned to the outer level."
        when ParseEmptyBlock -> "Add a statement, or use 'do:' for an empty body."
        when ParseMultipleStatements -> "Put each declaration or statement on its own line."
        when ParseLegacyAndSeparator -> "Since 0.10.0 'and' is the boolean operator (short-circuit). Separate arguments, parameters and struct fields with ',' — e.g. 'calling f with 1, 2', 'weave g with x as int, y as int', 'with x is 1, y is 2'. ('map of K to V' still uses 'to'.)"
        when ParseAtIndexPrecedence -> "Write 'set xs at (n - 1) is v' when the index is computed."
        when ParseMaxDepth -> "Split the expression into named intermediate values, or reduce the number of nested blocks."
        when ParseMaxBlockDepth -> "Flatten the block structure or split it into helper weaves."
        when ParseInvalidSetTarget -> "Assign to a name, a field, an index or 'essence of' a pointer."
        when ParseInvalidCallTarget -> "Write 'calling name', 'calling module.name' or 'calling .method'."
        when ParseInvalidAttribute -> "Use '@name' or '@name(arg, ...)'."
        when ParseInvalidDeclareParams -> "Use 'name as type' entries, optionally ending with '...'."
        when ParseInvalidWhenClause -> "Write 'when <pattern> [with <payload>] [if <guard>] -> <body>'."
        when ParseInvalidType -> "Check the type spelling."
        when ParseUnexpectedEof -> "Close the construct before the end of the file."

## Nota adicional del issue ("" si no tiene).
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un literal estático; no liberar.
weave parse_issue_note with issue as ParseIssue into string:
    return judge issue:
        when ParseExpectedToken -> "PenguScript is indentation-sensitive: statements in a block must be indented consistently."
        when ParseUnexpectedToken -> "PenguScript parses blocks by indentation; argument, parameter and field lists use ','."
        when ParseExpectedExpression -> ""
        when ParseExpectedType -> ""
        when ParseExpectedName -> "PenguScript identifiers are ASCII-only."
        when ParseExpectedNewline -> "A single-line block ('if c: return 0') is the only place where two statements share a line."
        when ParseExpectedIndent -> "A ':' that ends a line must be followed by an indented block."
        when ParseExpectedDedent -> ""
        when ParseEmptyBlock -> ""
        when ParseMultipleStatements -> ""
        when ParseLegacyAndSeparator -> "The old 'and' list separator was removed in 0.10.0; see the CHANGELOG migration notes."
        when ParseAtIndexPrecedence -> "'at' is a postfix operator, like '.field' or 'length': it takes a single atom as its index."
        when ParseMaxDepth -> "The parser, checker and C backend are recursive; the limit protects them from a stack overflow."
        when ParseMaxBlockDepth -> "Deeply nested blocks exceed the recursive front-end limit."
        when ParseInvalidSetTarget -> ""
        when ParseInvalidCallTarget -> ""
        when ParseInvalidAttribute -> ""
        when ParseInvalidDeclareParams -> ""
        when ParseInvalidWhenClause -> ""
        when ParseInvalidType -> ""
        when ParseUnexpectedEof -> ""

## Emite el diagnóstico de un issue en `[start, end)`.
##
## `detail` es prestado. El mensaje se construye y se libera aquí; el
## `DiagnosticBag` pasa a ser dueño del `Span` y de las copias internas.
##
## ## Memoria
## Asigna el mensaje y el diagnóstico; liberar el bag al final.
weave emit_parse_issue with bag as ref to diag.DiagnosticBag, src as ref to psource.SourceFile, issue as ParseIssue, start as int, end as int, detail as string into void:
    var s as pspan.ByteSpan is with start is start, end is end
    var msg as string is calling parse_issue_message with issue, detail
    defer banish msg
    var help as string is calling parse_issue_help with issue
    var note as string is calling parse_issue_note with issue
    calling psdiag.emit_error with bag, src, PSC_E_SYNTAX, msg, s, help, note
